        {
            "source_entity_instance": "2022 Pakistan floods",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Pakistan",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "The devastating floods in Pakistan in August 2022 appear to have been, at least in part, influenced by a MHW that occurred in the northern Arabian Sea. These catastrophic floods, caused by extreme precipitation events exceeding even the 99.9th percentile, affected approximately 33 million people in Pakistan and resulted in nearly 1500 fatalities (Nanditha et al. 2023).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "atmospheric heatwaves",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "China",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "While the 2022 Pakistan floods have been linked to the triple-dip La Ni\u00f1a (Jeong et al. 2023), atmospheric heatwaves over China and Europe (Hong et al. 2023), and atmospheric rivers (Nanditha et al. 2023), our findings emphasize the significant role of MHWs in the northern Arabian Sea in driving the extreme precipitation over Pakistan.",
